cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the two ggml applications its graph builders are copied from.
title: skin-tokens-ggml and pixal3d-ggml graph builders (copied for Gate 3)
abstract: >-
  The ggml graph builders Gate 3 (G3.graph, G3.cost) runs on random weights,
  copied function by function so the gate builds the apps' own op sequences
  without vendoring either app. From skin-tokens-ggml src/qwen.cpp: linear,
  rms, repeat_kv, repeat_kv_batched, qwen_graph_evaluator::cache_view and
  ::decode_layer, and the graph part of ::decode (embedding rows, the decoder
  layers, the final norm, the logits). From pixal3d-ggml trellis2.cpp:
  sdpa_auto (the flash-attention path), timestep_embedding, rope_tables and
  the graph of trellis2_ss_flow_forward (the stem, the shared modulation, the
  block body with its lin/modulate/rope/qk_norm lambdas, the head), and
  build_neighbor_indices and one level of shape_dec_run's graph (the child
  head, the ConvNeXt blocks and the up-block's part A, each submanifold 3^3
  conv as 27 x get_rows + mask mul + mul_mat).


  Adapted: the model lookups (weights_.tensor, m->tensors) are a name ->
  tensor function; decode_layer and decode take the KV caches and weights as
  parameters instead of evaluator members, and decode builds only the graph
  (allocation, inputs and readback are the caller's); the flow's lambdas are
  members of one struct shared by block() and forward(); sdpa_auto always
  takes the flash-attention path (the app's TRELLIS2_SDPA_EXACT switch is
  dropped); the DiT block gains Pixal3D's one change to TRELLIS.2's
  cross-attention, ProjectAttention's proj_linear(proj) added to the
  cross-attention output (V-Sekai-fire/Pixal3D cdbb2bb,
  pixal3d/modules/attention/proj_attention.py); the sparse level names its
  child-head up-block by this level's block count. Op sequences, shapes,
  epsilons and scales are the apps'.
